kind: profile
question: on the RTX 5090, which kernels hold the Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M decode step at depth 512 after the night's landings?
term: the nsys window wall of one decode step at depth 512, nsys-gpu.sh's table, Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M, generate_qwen3moe
  of main a5821c355
unit: ms
predict: 11.1..11.6
condition: one lease through nsys-gpu.sh; the RTX 5090 alone at 600 W, no other compute process
decide-in: rank the kernels by time against their bytes at 1.68 TB/s; open the largest gap as the next round
decide-below: under 11.1: the table's window is not the A/B's step; read the boundary lines first
decide-above: above 11.6: nsys moved the step; read the table for shares only
